@*
    Idiomatic Heddle -- composed-page (phase 9; authoring standard D16).

    Patterns followed, from Heddle's own documentation:
      Language reference   docs/language-reference.md ("Composition without coupling" --
                           the layout-as-definition idiom, Q1.7)
      Architecture         docs/architecture.md

    The page imports the definition-only layout and calls @layout() with the slider body; the
    body splices at the layout's @out() slot. The slider content is the SAME as the controlled
    track's -- the verifier's calibration pin (RemovedSegment = the slider fragment) fails an
    empty body, deliberately. Checked by the functional verifier, not the byte gate.
*@

@<<{{shared/layout.heddle}}
@layout()
{{
        <div class="slider-wrapper theme-default">
            <div id="slider" class="nivoSlider">
            </div>
            <div class="home-content">
                <div>
                    <a href="/products/gluten-free">
                        <img src="/files/homepage/homebtmbanners/gluten-hp.jpg" width="984" border="0" />
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
}}
